  "answer_text": "Here is how you can access your **My Service Canada Account (MSCA)**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd17 Direct Login Link\n\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Click here to sign in to My Service Canada Account (MSCA)](https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/services/my-account.html)**\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd11 Ways to Sign In\n\nYou have several options to log in to MSCA:\n\n1. **GCKey** \u2014 GCKey allows you to access multiple Government of Canada online services.\n\n2. **Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner** \u2014 Interac\u00ae Sign-In Partner allows you to register or sign in using your online banking sign-in information to access MSCA.\n\n3. **Provincial Sign-In** \u2014 You can access My Service Canada Account (MSCA) by signing in or registering with your provincial sign-in. This service is only available for residents of Alberta and British Columbia.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udcdd New User? How to Register\n\nIf you don't have an account yet, you'll need:\n- To create a GCKey username and password if you don't already have one, and a **Social Insurance Number (SIN)**.\n- A **Personal Access Code (PAC)** \u2014 PACs are used to verify your identity when registering for MSCA. If you already applied for CPP/OAS benefits, your PAC has been sent to you by mail.\n\n---\n\n## \u26a0\ufe0f Important Reminder\n\nYou must access and use MSCA only as yourself. No one is authorized to use or create an account on your behalf.\n\n---\n\nIf you're having trouble logging in, you can contact **Service Canada** at **1-800-O-Canada (1-800-622-6232)** for assistance.",
